279: ### Use Case Rate limit requests for teleTAN creation
280: To limit the damage in case an authorized client for teleTAN creation was compromised, the number of teleTANs created per time frame is limited. The limit for the component is global and applies to all users of the API endpoint for teleTAN creation. The limit and the time window are configurable.
281: 
282: In addition, a specific warning message is logged when the number of created teleTANs is above 80% of the limit.
283: 
284: The use case is part of the teleTAN creation use case.
285: 
286: Steps
287: 1. Count the number of created teleTAN in the current time window 
288: 2. If the number of created teleTANs is above 80% of the threshold log a specific warning message 
289: 3. If the number of created teleTANs is above the threshold return http 429
290: 
291: ### Use Case Allow component to be used in an internal only XOR external only mode
292: Based on configuration the component must be able to switch between an internal and external mode. 
293: External mode means that only the designated public available endpoints of the API are active 
294: and the internal ones (create teleTAN, verify TAN) are not active.
295: 
296: ### Use Case Plausible Deniablity for being positivly tested
297: To allow a client to implement Plausible Deniablity for being positivly tested the service needs to fullfill two 
298: changes acroos all API endpoints which are called by the mobile app. The use case takes the perspective of an attacking user which watches network traffic with regards to 
299: request/response size and timing.
